#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# airy_bi_prime

#% text
# `airy_bi_prime(x)` gives the derivative `Bi'(x)` of the Airy function.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `airy_bi_prime(0)` is `3^(1/6)/gamma(1/3)`. Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values.

#% item
# Its derivative is `x*airy_bi(x)` (DLMF 9.2.1).

#% item
# `airy_bi_prime` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
airy_bi_prime(0)
#% output
#= 3^(1/6)/gamma(1/3)

#% cell
airy_bi_prime(1.0)
#% output
#= 0.9324359333927756

#% cell
airy_bi_prime(-3.0)
#% output
#= -0.6756112226852585

#% cell
n(airy_bi_prime(1), 30)
#% output
#= 0.9324359333927756329594514536744353

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The derivative:

#% cell
d(airy_bi_prime(x), x)
#% output
#= x*airy_bi(x)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `airy_bi`, `airy_ai_prime`, `airy_ai`
